    DATABASE_CA_CERT setting takes Supabase's certificate so the connection is
    fully verified. I also found that an sslmode in the URL silently overrides
    the code's TLS settings, so the code now removes it from the URL when the
    certificate is set.
  - Cross-domain support: VITE_API_URL tells the frontend where the API lives
    (for both REST and sockets), and WEB_ORIGIN sets which web domains the API
    accepts requests from. Both are unset locally, so dev and ngrok behave
    exactly as before.
